## uic-modeler-mod21: fillet and chamfer of edges (modeling/fillet.rs, modeling/messages.rs)

uic-fillet-refused-no-edges = No edge to round or cut. Select edges, or faces with sharp edges.
uic-fillet-refused-not-solid = Fillet and Chamfer work on edges of a closed solid. Check Solid shows the open edges.
uic-fillet-refused-flat = An edge lies between faces in one plane. There is no corner to round or cut.
uic-fillet-refused-corner = A corner is not supported. Fillet and Chamfer work at corners of three faces, and not where convex and concave edges meet.
uic-fillet-refused-fit = The size does not fit. At most about { $most } mm fits.
uic-fillet-refused-no-room = The size does not fit. There is no room for it there.
uic-fillet-refused-small = The radius is too small for the segments. Use fewer segments or a larger radius.
uic-fillet-refused-segments = The number of segments must be from 1 to 64.
uic-fillet-refused-size = The size must be larger than 0.01 mm.
uic-fillet-refused-result = The result is not a valid solid, so nothing changed.
uic-fillet-refused-edges = The edit makes more new edges than one edit allows (10,000). Choose fewer edges, or round them in more than one step.
uic-fillet-refused-edges-segments = The edit makes more new edges than one edit allows (10,000). Use fewer segments: at most about { $most }.
uic-fillet-refused-scaled = The model is scaled unequally along its axes, so a round would not be round. Reset its scale first.
